\title{Notes on the dynamics of neurons}
\tag{notes}
\tag{math}
\tag{draft}
\tag{agent-draft}
\tag{fnip}
\author{utensil}
\date{2026-11-25}

\p{A recorded voltage is one coordinate of a neuron's state. The same
stimulus can arrive at different states and leave different traces, so
the object of study is the evolution of the state. The examples come
from neuron models. The statements are about flows, equilibria and
periodic orbits.}

\p{The notes begin with one planar model neuron. Its state is a point
of the plane, and a voltage trace is the membrane-potential coordinate
of that point.}

\transclude{fnip-0002}
